# PHASE 13 — TESTING AND VERIFICATION

After implementing changes:

1. Install dependencies reproducibly.
2. Run the actual linter.
3. Run TypeScript type checking.
4. Run the production build.
5. Run available unit or integration tests.
6. Fix errors caused by your changes.
7. Inspect the final diff.
8. Test every route that can reasonably be tested.
9. Verify that all image assets resolve in the production build.
10. Test the contact form states without claiming that real delivery works unless an actual configured submission has been verified.
11. Test keyboard navigation, focus states, dialogs and form validation.
12. Test responsive layouts using a real browser or automated browser tooling if available.
13. Check for console errors, missing resources and horizontal overflow.
14. Use Lighthouse or comparable accessibility/performance tooling where available.
15. Record tests that could not be performed.

At minimum, verify the 320px, 360px, 390px, 768px, 1024px, 1280px and 1440px viewport widths using browser testing when the environment supports it.

If browser testing or the network is unavailable, continue with all static checks that can be performed. Report the limitation honestly rather than declaring an untested result successful.

